  "content": "The v6 Reactor provides `RelationalDbProcessor<DB>` as a base class for processors that need database access. Key features: `getNamespace(driveId)` static method creates per-drive database isolation preventing data collisions; `initAndUpgrade()` lifecycle hook runs migrations on startup; `this.relationalDb` provides a typed Kysely instance; `query(driveId, relationalDb)` static method enables querying from subgraphs. The factory creates namespaced stores via `module.relationalDb.createNamespace<T>(namespace)`. Scaffolding is generated with `ph generate processor --name <name> --type relationalDb --document-types <type>`.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
